From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] fix: text direction and alignment also work when the selection holds inline code
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 1.0 (2026-10-16)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0023)

Problem: a line that starts with inline code (e.g. `Ctrl` + Persian text) could
not be made right-to-left. With the whole line selected, the menu showed
"Right to left" (patch 0021) but choosing it did nothing; selecting only the
Persian part after the code worked.

Cause: setTextDirection and setTextAlignment returned false whenever
isInCode(state) was true, and that is also true when the selection only touches
inline code. Patch 0021 fixed the menu, not the commands.

Fix: both commands stop only inside a code block (isInCode with onlyBlock).

Files (2; M = modified):
  M shared/editor/extensions/TextDirection.ts
  M shared/editor/extensions/TextAlignment.ts

---
---

diff --git a/shared/editor/extensions/TextDirection.ts b/shared/editor/extensions/TextDirection.ts
--- a/shared/editor/extensions/TextDirection.ts
+++ b/shared/editor/extensions/TextDirection.ts
@@ -69,7 +69,9 @@
    */
   private setTextDirection(dir: Direction | null): Command {
     return (state, dispatch) => {
-      if (isInCode(state)) {
+      // KMS patch 0024: only a code block stops the command. Inline code in the
+      // selection (e.g. `Ctrl` at the start of a line) must not.
+      if (isInCode(state, { onlyBlock: true })) {
         return false;
       }
 
diff --git a/shared/editor/extensions/TextAlignment.ts b/shared/editor/extensions/TextAlignment.ts
--- a/shared/editor/extensions/TextAlignment.ts
+++ b/shared/editor/extensions/TextAlignment.ts
@@ -55,7 +55,9 @@
    */
   private setTextAlignment(align: TextAlign | null): Command {
     return (state, dispatch) => {
-      if (isInCode(state)) {
+      // KMS patch 0024: only a code block stops the command. Inline code in the
+      // selection (e.g. `Ctrl` at the start of a line) must not.
+      if (isInCode(state, { onlyBlock: true })) {
         return false;
       }
 
